1
00:00:00,293 --> 00:00:06,010
[Filing For Love]

2
00:00:11,793 --> 00:00:14,404
So they're still waiting at the ER?

3
00:00:17,418 --> 00:00:20,060
No, you don't have to. I'll call again later.

4
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:22,077
Just let me out here.

5
00:00:22,077 --> 00:00:24,318
You're still pretty far.
Just past the intersection...

6
00:00:24,318 --> 00:00:27,043
In Ah... In Ah!

7
00:01:44,752 --> 00:01:46,688
Excuse me, hold on a second.

8
00:01:46,688 --> 00:01:48,482
Wasn't surgery supposed to start right away?

9
00:01:48,482 --> 00:01:49,691
What's the holdup here?

10
00:01:49,691 --> 00:01:52,611
Hold on a moment, please.

11
00:01:54,543 --> 00:01:56,479
Is our OR still not ready?

12
00:01:56,479 --> 00:01:59,253
Everything's full.
The last one got taken by a VIP case.

13
00:01:59,253 --> 00:02:00,285
What is it?

14
00:02:00,285 --> 00:02:03,660
What about a switch or backup team, then?

15
00:02:03,660 --> 00:02:07,476
You can't just leave him like that.
Do something!

16
00:02:08,293 --> 00:02:10,061
In Ah.

17
00:02:10,953 --> 00:02:12,672
You can pull strings, right?

18
00:02:12,672 --> 00:02:14,424
Make a call to Haemu Hospital, please?

19
00:02:14,424 --> 00:02:17,678
Please, I'm begging you. Help me out?

20
00:02:21,556 --> 00:02:23,850
[Surgery Time]

21
00:02:23,850 --> 00:02:25,480
[Surgery Time, Current Time, Anesthesia Time]

22
00:02:39,376 --> 00:02:43,954
Rest easy. Professor Yoon is
the top trauma surgeon around.

23
00:02:43,954 --> 00:02:46,456
I'll be watching this through till the end.

24
00:02:46,456 --> 00:02:47,749
Thank you, Director.

25
00:02:47,749 --> 00:02:49,517
I'll be off.

26
00:02:56,168 --> 00:02:58,817
[Operating Room]

27
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:32,793
Are you awake?

28
00:04:32,793 --> 00:04:34,622
Hey.

29
00:05:01,571 --> 00:05:05,210
[Episode 8: Wanting and Resenting]

30
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:09,918
Catch me if you can.

31
00:05:15,835 --> 00:05:18,316
What is this, a kids' playground?

32
00:05:18,316 --> 00:05:20,777
Hello, patient here.

33
00:05:20,777 --> 00:05:24,139
Just let me rest, please, okay?

34
00:05:24,139 --> 00:05:27,119
Hey, we splurged on this for you,
and you won't even eat?

35
00:05:27,119 --> 00:05:30,460
Forget it. Nothing tastes good right now.
You three finish it.

36
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:33,457
Oh, poor baby, no appetite?

37
00:05:33,457 --> 00:05:34,619
Tell me if anything sounds good.

38
00:05:34,619 --> 00:05:36,292
I'll make it for you on the spot.

39
00:05:36,292 --> 00:05:37,752
Hey, by the way, lately...

40
00:05:37,752 --> 00:05:39,630
That woman hasn't shown up?

41
00:05:40,547 --> 00:05:41,958
You know, Ms. Joo!

42
00:05:41,958 --> 00:05:43,049
Right?

43
00:05:43,049 --> 00:05:45,626
She was here all the time
when you were knocked out.

44
00:05:45,626 --> 00:05:48,597
Staring at you with this tender look.

45
00:05:48,597 --> 00:05:51,350
But now that you're awake, not once?

46
00:05:51,350 --> 00:05:55,662
Maybe his energy comes back when she shows up?

47
00:05:55,662 --> 00:05:58,477
Your consciousness came back
while she was here, remember?

48
00:05:59,524 --> 00:06:01,382
What's going on between you two?

49
00:06:01,382 --> 00:06:03,562
Doesn't look like just a coworker thing.

50
00:06:03,562 --> 00:06:06,114
Something's up, right?

51
00:06:06,114 --> 00:06:10,259
Are you guys more than just boss and employee?

52
00:06:12,002 --> 00:06:15,624
Drop it already. Seriously, please.

53
00:06:15,624 --> 00:06:18,360
Are you getting shy?

54
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:22,381
Look at you, so cute.

55
00:06:22,381 --> 00:06:24,050
Quit it. Come on.

56
00:07:12,931 --> 00:07:14,628
Smells amazing.

57
00:07:25,877 --> 00:07:28,404
What is this? Am I your trained puppy?

58
00:07:28,404 --> 00:07:30,406
Toast delivery at the crack of dawn?

59
00:07:30,406 --> 00:07:32,700
Hey, you still came, though.

60
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:34,283
Fear brought me here, fear.

61
00:07:34,283 --> 00:07:36,674
Who sends twenty-plus texts
for one piece of toast?

62
00:07:36,674 --> 00:07:37,747
Well, then...

63
00:07:37,747 --> 00:07:40,002
What scared you so much
when I was still out cold?

64
00:07:40,002 --> 00:07:42,418
Coming by day and night every single day.

65
00:07:42,418 --> 00:07:44,777
Taking such devoted care of me?

66
00:07:46,643 --> 00:07:49,134
My sisters spilled everything.

67
00:07:49,134 --> 00:07:51,855
Said it was heartbreaking
to watch from the side.

68
00:07:54,543 --> 00:07:56,175
Fear, yeah.

69
00:07:58,585 --> 00:08:00,120
It really got to me.

70
00:08:02,335 --> 00:08:05,626
And as your superior...

71
00:08:05,626 --> 00:08:07,986
Protecting my staff means checking the status.

72
00:08:07,986 --> 00:08:10,213
Dead or alive, you know.

73
00:08:21,835 --> 00:08:26,431
Right, purely staff protection.

74
00:08:26,431 --> 00:08:29,450
While you're at it with the staff protection...

75
00:08:29,450 --> 00:08:32,067
Discharge me too, why don't you?

76
00:08:33,011 --> 00:08:34,444
Me?

77
00:08:34,444 --> 00:08:35,743
Yeah.

78
00:08:42,186 --> 00:08:44,418
Easy, easy with that.

79
00:08:44,418 --> 00:08:46,483
Lots of breakables in there.

80
00:08:46,483 --> 00:08:49,960
Stuck in one hospital room
and somehow your stuff multiplied?

81
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:53,255
Turns out deliveries reach the room just fine.

82
00:08:57,411 --> 00:09:00,005
What in the world am I even doing right now?

83
00:09:00,872 --> 00:09:03,902
Why's discharging you falling on me?

84
00:09:03,902 --> 00:09:05,877
The stitches in my abs haven't come out yet.

85
00:09:05,877 --> 00:09:09,002
This stuff is heavy,
and nobody else is picking me up.

86
00:09:09,002 --> 00:09:12,358
Isn't this exactly
when staff protection kicks in?

87
00:09:14,177 --> 00:09:15,428
Just you wait.

88
00:09:15,428 --> 00:09:16,752
The second those stitches come out...

89
00:09:16,752 --> 00:09:18,306
your labor is mine.

90
00:09:18,306 --> 00:09:20,793
I'll squeeze every last drop out of you.

91
00:09:20,793 --> 00:09:22,393
Got it.

92
00:09:22,393 --> 00:09:24,271
See, that's what I'm saying.

93
00:09:24,271 --> 00:09:27,190
That whole area is
seriously undervalued right now.

94
00:09:27,190 --> 00:09:29,359
People might say it's old development talk.

95
00:09:29,359 --> 00:09:31,376
But land never lets you down.

96
00:09:31,376 --> 00:09:33,376
Sure thing.

97
00:09:33,376 --> 00:09:36,074
<i>You can't just leave him like that.
Do something!</i>

98
00:09:36,074 --> 00:09:38,746
<i>Please, I'm begging you. Help me out?</i>

99
00:09:42,209 --> 00:09:43,674
Right, brother?

100
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:46,976
We'll see.

101
00:09:48,079 --> 00:09:51,089
Anyway, this guy always misses the timing.

102
00:09:51,089 --> 00:09:54,968
He isn't keen on tearing that place down.

103
00:09:54,968 --> 00:09:58,182
Lots of folks would lose
their livelihoods, I suppose.

104
00:09:58,182 --> 00:09:59,749
Compensation's on the table.

105
00:09:59,749 --> 00:10:01,678
Nobody's just kicking people out.

106
00:10:01,678 --> 00:10:05,354
Yeah well, my big brother's got a soft heart.

107
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:08,398
Since we were kids,
he couldn't walk past anyone struggling.

108
00:10:08,398 --> 00:10:11,693
Always giving in, sacrificing.

109
00:10:11,693 --> 00:10:14,079
Our family's been tough for generations...
you know my old man, right?

110
00:10:14,079 --> 00:10:16,922
The fiercest man in all of Korea.

111
00:10:18,617 --> 00:10:21,438
Beats me who my brother takes after.

112
00:10:21,438 --> 00:10:23,330
One thing's certain.

113
00:10:23,330 --> 00:10:25,307
It isn't Dad's side.

114
00:10:26,543 --> 00:10:29,143
Has to be Mom's, definitely Mom's.

115
00:10:48,752 --> 00:10:50,293
Sorry about that.

116
00:10:50,293 --> 00:10:51,293
I'll apologize for him.

117
00:10:51,293 --> 00:10:53,417
He's had way too much to drink.

118
00:10:54,335 --> 00:10:56,543
PR's been contacted. Get the car ready.

119
00:10:56,543 --> 00:10:58,964
I'll bring him down right now.

120
00:11:11,585 --> 00:11:13,681
Ah Jeong, you made it.

121
00:11:13,681 --> 00:11:15,898
Why are you acting out of character?

122
00:11:17,429 --> 00:11:20,767
The board meeting is right around the corner.
How can you be this reckless?

123
00:11:22,002 --> 00:11:24,311
Cut me some slack today.

124
00:11:32,793 --> 00:11:34,350
Joo In Ah.

125
00:11:34,990 --> 00:11:38,379
What exactly is that woman to you?

126
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:43,175
The woman I'd die alongside.

127
00:11:50,221 --> 00:11:53,647
Seriously, not one emergency umbrella
in this car?

128
00:11:54,376 --> 00:11:57,898
I'll have to stash one in here next time.

129
00:12:00,469 --> 00:12:04,055
If Ah Jeong's home,
why not ask her to bring an umbrella?

130
00:12:04,055 --> 00:12:06,442
No need to go that far...

131
00:12:06,442 --> 00:12:09,618
Looks like a quick shower.
I'll just sit it out.

132
00:12:14,209 --> 00:12:16,543
So why did things end with Ah Jeong?

133
00:12:17,277 --> 00:12:18,749
The reason's a mystery to me, too.

134
00:12:18,749 --> 00:12:21,085
She just up and ghosted me one day.

135
00:12:21,085 --> 00:12:22,698
Didn't you ask her why?

136
00:12:22,698 --> 00:12:24,626
You must have run into her at work.

137
00:12:24,626 --> 00:12:26,218
Never asked.

138
00:12:27,078 --> 00:12:29,382
She kept quiet for a reason.

139
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:35,233
What?

140
00:12:35,879 --> 00:12:39,663
Would you have pressed her till the end?

141
00:12:41,752 --> 00:12:43,960
If it were me...

142
00:12:43,960 --> 00:12:46,249
If I were in Ah Jeong's shoes...

143
00:12:47,742 --> 00:12:49,889
That's probably what I'd have wanted.

144
00:12:52,854 --> 00:12:55,774
There's this weird thing
where at crucial moments...

145
00:12:55,774 --> 00:12:57,960
I end up hiding what I really feel.

146
00:12:58,929 --> 00:13:00,999
And at the same time...

147
00:13:01,626 --> 00:13:04,782
Part of me wishes
someone would drag me out of it.

148
00:13:04,782 --> 00:13:07,995
Refuse to give up on me no matter what.

149
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:11,138
A selfish, contradictory feeling
like that creeps in.

150
00:13:13,752 --> 00:13:18,062
Why not just lay it all out honestly then?

151
00:13:21,251 --> 00:13:22,967
<i>Are you serious?</i>

152
00:13:22,967 --> 00:13:25,770
<i>So I should go through with this marriage?</i>

153
00:13:25,770 --> 00:13:27,290
<i>Yeah, dead serious.</i>

154
00:13:27,290 --> 00:13:30,202
<i>What's the alternative, run away together?</i>

155
00:13:30,202 --> 00:13:33,436
<i>Kicked out of home, stripped of everything?</i>

156
00:13:33,436 --> 00:13:35,070
<i>That's not the life I want.</i>

157
00:13:35,070 --> 00:13:37,696
<i>- In Ah.
- And besides...</i>

158
00:13:37,696 --> 00:13:41,085
<i>Naive thoughts about us lasting forever?</i>

159
00:13:41,085 --> 00:13:43,209
<i>Never crossed my mind, not even once.</i>

160
00:13:43,209 --> 00:13:46,325
<i>So drop the guilt
and walk away with a clear head.</i>

161
00:13:46,325 --> 00:13:48,452
<i>Honestly, I'm...</i>

162
00:13:48,452 --> 00:13:50,469
<i>Truly fine.</i>

163
00:13:57,044 --> 00:13:58,625
Probably...

164
00:13:58,625 --> 00:14:01,804
The truth is I don't know how to be happy.

165
00:14:05,835 --> 00:14:09,408
The moment something feels like happiness,
anxiety creeps in.

166
00:14:09,408 --> 00:14:12,293
Am I really someone who deserves this?

167
00:14:12,293 --> 00:14:13,894
Fear takes over.

168
00:14:13,894 --> 00:14:16,011
And I hide, retreat.

169
00:14:17,188 --> 00:14:19,791
Misery feels safe and cozy, after all.

170
00:14:26,626 --> 00:14:28,213
Close your eyes.

171
00:14:28,992 --> 00:14:30,966
Why?

172
00:14:30,966 --> 00:14:34,290
Nothing weird, I promise. Just close them.

173
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:38,961
There.

174
00:14:39,952 --> 00:14:42,020
What do you hear?

175
00:14:42,626 --> 00:14:44,174
Rain, obviously.

176
00:14:44,174 --> 00:14:47,501
Calm down and really focus on it, alright?

177
00:15:01,602 --> 00:15:04,986
Raindrops hitting the windshield.

178
00:15:04,986 --> 00:15:06,960
And?

179
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,306
And?

180
00:15:09,407 --> 00:15:10,741
The car engine running.

181
00:15:10,741 --> 00:15:12,002
And?

182
00:15:15,002 --> 00:15:17,549
A motorcycle going by outside.

183
00:15:18,571 --> 00:15:19,939
And?

184
00:15:24,626 --> 00:15:26,103
Kids...

185
00:15:26,757 --> 00:15:28,439
laughing in the distance.

186
00:15:29,151 --> 00:15:30,455
And?

187
00:15:33,514 --> 00:15:35,808
Your breathing.

188
00:15:35,808 --> 00:15:37,103
And?

189
00:15:42,585 --> 00:15:44,478
My heart beating.

190
00:15:49,543 --> 00:15:52,007
That's how you feel it.

191
00:15:54,201 --> 00:15:55,884
Happiness,

192
00:15:55,884 --> 00:15:58,247
when you pour your whole heart into it.

193
00:15:58,247 --> 00:16:00,766
And look quietly inside.

194
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:05,130
It's right there inside you, for sure.

195
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:07,549
It's always sitting there.

196
00:16:07,549 --> 00:16:09,489
Whenever you want to find it,

197
00:16:11,209 --> 00:16:13,309
find it just like this.

198
00:16:44,919 --> 00:16:46,710
Glad to have you back.

199
00:16:46,710 --> 00:16:47,922
You've been through a lot.

200
00:16:47,922 --> 00:16:50,174
Thank you.

201
00:16:50,174 --> 00:16:52,137
You went through a lot.

202
00:16:52,137 --> 00:16:54,095
But your face is

203
00:16:54,095 --> 00:16:55,514
looking better.

204
00:16:55,514 --> 00:16:57,710
Hospital food must have agreed with you.

205
00:16:57,710 --> 00:17:00,309
Skipping the office does wonders
for the complexion, doesn't it?

206
00:17:00,309 --> 00:17:02,061
Oh, come on now.

207
00:17:02,061 --> 00:17:04,564
His face was always sharp to begin with.

208
00:17:04,564 --> 00:17:07,266
The whole Audit Office lit up with you back.

209
00:17:07,266 --> 00:17:09,085
Glad to have you back.

210
00:17:09,085 --> 00:17:12,572
I really missed you so much.

211
00:17:12,572 --> 00:17:14,658
Tone it down, way too much.

212
00:17:14,658 --> 00:17:16,851
Don't worry about Mr. Ahn one bit.

213
00:17:16,851 --> 00:17:19,742
Legal is hammering away at this right now.

214
00:17:19,742 --> 00:17:21,113
He's going down hard, count on it.

215
00:17:21,113 --> 00:17:23,476
Word is, even his family cut him loose.

216
00:17:23,476 --> 00:17:24,584
Reaping what he sowed, plain and simple.

217
00:17:24,584 --> 00:17:26,001
You've been through a lot.

218
00:17:26,001 --> 00:17:27,015
Yes.

219
00:17:27,015 --> 00:17:29,171
Hey, Team 3 sure adores you.

220
00:17:29,171 --> 00:17:31,549
Boy, were you ever against going at first.

221
00:17:31,549 --> 00:17:32,789
No, you were dying to go.

222
00:17:32,789 --> 00:17:34,531
Yeah, totally itching for it.

223
00:17:34,531 --> 00:17:37,055
Yeah, that's right.

224
00:17:37,055 --> 00:17:39,043
Good day, Ms. Joo.

225
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:43,094
Good to have you back.

226
00:17:43,094 --> 00:17:44,603
Yes. Good to be back.

227
00:17:44,603 --> 00:17:47,314
Do you have any plans for today?

228
00:17:47,314 --> 00:17:50,667
Almost didn't recognize you.
You're glowing more than usual.

229
00:17:53,905 --> 00:17:57,117
What, was I gloomy before or something?

230
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:59,368
No, that's not what I meant...

231
00:17:59,368 --> 00:18:01,454
Something good must be in the air, huh?

232
00:18:01,454 --> 00:18:03,832
Like a favorite staff member's comeback maybe?

233
00:18:03,832 --> 00:18:06,664
- Such a warm welcome rolled out for me...
- Mr. Noh.

234
00:18:08,793 --> 00:18:12,719
Looks like a long absence
dulled your office instincts.

235
00:18:16,809 --> 00:18:19,297
Better whip those back into shape fast.

236
00:18:25,979 --> 00:18:28,564
She still can't stand you, it seems.

237
00:18:28,564 --> 00:18:32,277
All that fighting
through the injury for nothing, sad.

238
00:18:35,835 --> 00:18:37,376
Hey, no problem.

239
00:18:37,376 --> 00:18:39,241
This much is nothing.

240
00:18:39,241 --> 00:18:42,418
Noh Ki Jun, Audit Office ace right here.

241
00:18:42,418 --> 00:18:44,126
Thanks.

242
00:18:44,126 --> 00:18:46,515
All right, let's do this.

243
00:19:11,066 --> 00:19:14,860
<i>Every assignment you handed over is done.</i>

244
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:16,195
[Audit Office, Head Joo In Ah]

245
00:19:16,195 --> 00:19:17,422
[Okey-dokey]

246
00:19:18,727 --> 00:19:21,174
Okey-dokey?

247
00:19:24,705 --> 00:19:26,918
That's harsh.

248
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:33,856
[That's harsh]
First day back from being sick and...

249
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:39,594
<i>Hard work earns a meal. I'll treat you.</i>

250
00:19:39,594 --> 00:19:40,639
<i>For real?</i>

251
00:19:40,639 --> 00:19:42,221
<i>When?</i>

252
00:19:42,221 --> 00:19:44,639
[Audit Office, Head Joo In Ah]

253
00:19:57,237 --> 00:20:00,588
<i>Friday evening. Come to my place.</i>

254
00:20:05,912 --> 00:20:07,631
What's wrong?

255
00:20:10,044 --> 00:20:12,893
My back is killing me.

256
00:20:35,335 --> 00:20:37,108
Mr. Noh.

257
00:20:37,108 --> 00:20:39,029
Hey, Doo Gi.

258
00:20:39,029 --> 00:20:42,741
Sorry I never made it to visit
while you were laid up.

259
00:20:42,741 --> 00:20:44,599
No big deal.

260
00:20:44,599 --> 00:20:46,160
If you took a stab wound...

261
00:20:46,160 --> 00:20:49,418
visiting wouldn't be on my list either,
so we're even.

262
00:20:49,418 --> 00:20:51,640
Come on, that's harsh.

263
00:20:52,666 --> 00:20:54,000
By the way...

264
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:56,771
Got a work thing I wanted to run by you.

265
00:20:57,419 --> 00:20:59,440
Haemu Pharma was your last beat, right?

266
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,639
Yeah, it was.

267
00:21:00,639 --> 00:21:04,126
Anything in particular
you were digging into back then?

268
00:21:04,126 --> 00:21:05,877
What are you talking about?

269
00:21:05,877 --> 00:21:07,015
The handover was complete.

270
00:21:07,015 --> 00:21:09,115
Didn't you check the cloud folder?

271
00:21:09,933 --> 00:21:10,983
Yeah.

272
00:21:10,983 --> 00:21:13,063
Nothing in there caught my eye.

273
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:14,294
Empty?

274
00:21:14,294 --> 00:21:15,956
Right.

275
00:21:17,926 --> 00:21:19,795
Let me look into it and circle back.

276
00:21:19,795 --> 00:21:21,753
- Got it.
- Right.

277
00:21:30,319 --> 00:21:33,076
<i>A subsidiary audit case was
sitting on my desk, a big one.</i>

278
00:21:33,076 --> 00:21:34,480
<i>Let me see it through to the end.</i>

279
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:36,688
<i>Get the files squared away
on the department cloud.</i>

280
00:21:36,688 --> 00:21:39,145
<i>Once that's done,
I'll review and handle the handover.</i>

281
00:21:42,925 --> 00:21:46,220
[Handover]

282
00:21:46,245 --> 00:21:48,207
[No search results were found for files
and folders related to Noh Ki Jun Handover]

283
00:21:57,752 --> 00:22:00,192
Jae Hong, you slammed right now?

284
00:22:00,192 --> 00:22:02,209
Listen, I need a favor.

285
00:22:02,209 --> 00:22:06,339
A file I uploaded to the department cloud
just vanished into thin air.

286
00:22:14,918 --> 00:22:17,809
Oh, perfect.

287
00:22:27,918 --> 00:22:29,658
What can I get you?

288
00:22:29,658 --> 00:22:33,017
For someone bouncing back from being sick...

289
00:22:33,017 --> 00:22:35,018
what dish helps with the recovery?

290
00:22:35,018 --> 00:22:36,143
Korean beef is the way.

291
00:22:36,143 --> 00:22:38,382
What's on the menu?

292
00:22:38,382 --> 00:22:41,335
Something easy that looks impressive...

293
00:22:41,335 --> 00:22:45,059
simple but with a sophisticated touch?

294
00:22:45,059 --> 00:22:47,819
Just pack up everything on display here.

295
00:22:47,819 --> 00:22:50,209
- All of it?
- Practice runs are part of the plan.

296
00:22:50,209 --> 00:22:51,968
Got it.

297
00:23:01,253 --> 00:23:04,489
<i>That folder was deleted two days later.</i>

298
00:23:04,489 --> 00:23:06,775
The trace points to Joo In Ah's PC.

299
00:23:21,774 --> 00:23:25,328
[Haemu Pharma]

300
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:29,078
[Requires Review: Haemu Pharma]

301
00:23:40,668 --> 00:23:42,711
<i>Whole garlic cloves, here we go.</i>

302
00:23:42,711 --> 00:23:45,085
<i>These are getting sliced in half too.</i>

303
00:23:45,085 --> 00:23:47,841
<i>Slicing them too thin kills the flavor.</i>

304
00:23:47,841 --> 00:23:51,136
<i>Keep them chunky and pile on the garlic.</i>

305
00:23:51,136 --> 00:23:55,183
<i>Eating it that way is good
for your health on top of it.</i>

306
00:24:04,668 --> 00:24:06,193
<i>Set the wok on the table.</i>

307
00:24:06,193 --> 00:24:10,376
<i>- A few drops of sesame oil will do.</i>
- Oil first...

308
00:24:10,376 --> 00:24:13,668
<i>- One spoon of garlic going in.</i>
- Oil...

309
00:24:13,668 --> 00:24:16,386
Oil's missing here, oil...

310
00:25:12,293 --> 00:25:15,361
This tastes incredible, oh my.

311
00:25:26,517 --> 00:25:27,896
Hey.

312
00:25:28,924 --> 00:25:30,834
In this early?

313
00:25:31,695 --> 00:25:33,829
Or did you skip going home altogether?

314
00:25:40,002 --> 00:25:43,188
What's going on?

315
00:25:47,251 --> 00:25:49,438
Back on your very first day here,

316
00:25:51,576 --> 00:25:54,469
what was the real reason
you pushed me to Team 3?

317
00:26:02,033 --> 00:26:05,354
Still bitter about the PM assignment?

318
00:26:05,354 --> 00:26:08,941
PM work, by my read, is no small matter.

319
00:26:08,941 --> 00:26:10,952
You've done it firsthand,
so the weight of it must've registered.

320
00:26:10,952 --> 00:26:14,823
How much the private bleeds
into the professional.

321
00:26:14,823 --> 00:26:17,630
Emotions are tangled in,
which makes handling it tricky.

322
00:26:18,228 --> 00:26:20,287
Someone like you,

323
00:26:20,287 --> 00:26:24,896
with that confidence and sharpness of yours,
untouched by what others think,

324
00:26:24,896 --> 00:26:26,349
the call was that you'd pull it off.

325
00:26:26,349 --> 00:26:27,962
Turned out the call was right.

326
00:26:33,335 --> 00:26:35,335
That's the whole of it?

327
00:26:35,335 --> 00:26:36,861
Any other reason?

328
00:26:38,543 --> 00:26:40,220
Nothing else, truly?

329
00:26:47,854 --> 00:26:49,543
[Special Audit Report on Sponsorships
and Governance of J Care Foundation]

330
00:26:49,543 --> 00:26:51,668
J Care Foundation.

331
00:26:51,668 --> 00:26:55,656
Haemu Pharma backs this medical entity
under their CSR initiative.

332
00:26:55,656 --> 00:26:57,239
On its face, nothing wrong there.

333
00:26:57,239 --> 00:27:00,075
Funding hits the place generously, though.

334
00:27:00,075 --> 00:27:03,587
A legal entity with zero name recognition,
zero track record.

335
00:27:07,832 --> 00:27:09,877
So I dug.

336
00:27:09,877 --> 00:27:13,505
Followed the trail, layer after layer,
doggedly all the way down.

337
00:27:13,505 --> 00:27:17,478
[J Care Foundation]

338
00:27:17,478 --> 00:27:19,929
The structure was twisted
into knots, ridiculously so.

339
00:27:19,929 --> 00:27:20,771
[J Care Foundation]

340
00:27:22,074 --> 00:27:25,008
At the end of the line,
the real owner of this entity is...

341
00:27:28,437 --> 00:27:30,844
Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol.

342
00:27:30,844 --> 00:27:33,233
This entity,

343
00:27:33,233 --> 00:27:35,951
Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol founded it,
didn't he?

344
00:27:42,805 --> 00:27:44,746
The floor is yours now.

345
00:27:44,746 --> 00:27:46,707
Is there a connection?

346
00:27:46,707 --> 00:27:50,311
Between this
and the reason I had to be moved to Team 3.

347
00:27:53,585 --> 00:27:54,671
<i>Alright.</i>

348
00:27:54,671 --> 00:27:57,315
<i>Your position needs adjusting.</i>

349
00:28:01,159 --> 00:28:04,558
[Noh Ki Jun Audit Team 1 Handover]

350
00:28:04,558 --> 00:28:05,646
[Permanent Deletion]

351
00:28:08,382 --> 00:28:10,979
[Delete Noh Ki Jun Audit Team 1 Handover
and all subfolders for good?]

352
00:28:10,979 --> 00:28:13,026
[Noh Ki Jun Audit Team 1 Handover file
has been permanently deleted]

353
00:28:15,944 --> 00:28:18,544
Pulling the plug on the investigation,
yes, that was me.

354
00:28:20,741 --> 00:28:23,617
But the Vice Chairman pocketing personal gain,

355
00:28:23,617 --> 00:28:25,555
or anything off
in Haemu Pharma's internal process,

356
00:28:25,555 --> 00:28:27,049
my read was that none of it held up.

357
00:28:27,049 --> 00:28:28,793
But that kind of...

358
00:28:28,793 --> 00:28:32,035
judgment call shouldn't
sit on your shoulders alone.

359
00:28:32,035 --> 00:28:36,710
Reporting up, putting it before the board,
running a special investigation,

360
00:28:36,710 --> 00:28:38,340
isn't that the order of business here?

361
00:28:38,340 --> 00:28:40,886
The substance and the fallout
would've blown out of proportion,

362
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:43,987
- with everyone turning into political pawns...
- The damage would've landed

363
00:28:43,987 --> 00:28:46,280
on Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol.

364
00:28:51,940 --> 00:28:55,285
Did some kind of favor come your way from him?

365
00:28:56,066 --> 00:28:58,270
He has no clue I even know.

366
00:29:06,668 --> 00:29:08,460
A person as airtight as you

367
00:29:08,460 --> 00:29:10,163
with the line between work
and personal drawn crystal clear,

368
00:29:10,163 --> 00:29:12,947
worried that Jeon Jae Yeol might take a hit,

369
00:29:12,947 --> 00:29:16,310
buried an issue like this by your own hand?

370
00:29:19,243 --> 00:29:22,551
Even if I drop it,
the lid's coming off eventually, so...

371
00:29:22,551 --> 00:29:24,793
one way or the other,

372
00:29:24,793 --> 00:29:27,222
true to who you are,

373
00:29:27,222 --> 00:29:29,480
set the record straight, please.

374
00:29:36,277 --> 00:29:37,318
Mr. Noh.

375
00:29:37,318 --> 00:29:39,893
- In early today.
- Good morning.

376
00:29:39,893 --> 00:29:42,253
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

377
00:30:19,432 --> 00:30:21,144
This feels good.

378
00:30:21,144 --> 00:30:22,705
Refreshing.

379
00:30:30,993 --> 00:30:32,837
You're home?

380
00:30:34,867 --> 00:30:36,510
You're late today.

381
00:30:41,804 --> 00:30:45,036
Hey, have you been drinking?

382
00:31:33,368 --> 00:31:35,093
Yes, Chairperson,

383
00:31:35,093 --> 00:31:37,026
this is Joo In Ah.

384
00:31:38,555 --> 00:31:42,031
There's an additional item to be reported
at tomorrow's board meeting.

385
00:31:45,743 --> 00:31:50,276
The final motion just passed as well.

386
00:31:54,076 --> 00:31:57,296
Head of Audit, would you like to speak?

387
00:31:58,050 --> 00:32:01,785
There's something
the Audit Committee didn't get to earlier

388
00:32:01,785 --> 00:32:04,164
that I'd like to bring before the board now.

389
00:32:04,164 --> 00:32:06,583
Hold on for a second.

390
00:32:06,583 --> 00:32:10,184
Since this wasn't on the agenda in advance,

391
00:32:12,410 --> 00:32:15,803
Director Park Sang Hwan apparently
has something to propose.

392
00:32:15,803 --> 00:32:17,094
The floor is yours.

393
00:32:17,094 --> 00:32:18,804
Yes.

394
00:32:18,804 --> 00:32:22,497
Please bear with me
for raising this so abruptly.

395
00:32:23,765 --> 00:32:25,739
Due to health concerns,

396
00:32:25,739 --> 00:32:26,977
our Chairman

397
00:32:26,977 --> 00:32:30,364
is currently limited
in carrying out official duties.

398
00:32:30,364 --> 00:32:33,942
As a result,
a great deal of key executive decisions

399
00:32:33,942 --> 00:32:38,358
have been falling
on Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol alone.

400
00:32:38,358 --> 00:32:41,032
Yet the Chairman remains in good standing,

401
00:32:41,032 --> 00:32:43,994
and nothing has changed
about him being our symbolic leader

402
00:32:43,994 --> 00:32:48,665
and the spiritual pillar of this group.

403
00:32:48,665 --> 00:32:50,194
With that in mind,

404
00:32:50,194 --> 00:32:52,919
to promote sharper decision-making

405
00:32:52,919 --> 00:32:56,186
and a more stable management environment,

406
00:32:57,618 --> 00:32:59,592
I'd like to put forward MD Jeon Seong Yeol

407
00:32:59,592 --> 00:33:03,920
for appointment as Co-Vice Chairman.

408
00:33:13,243 --> 00:33:15,702
What's wrong with Director Park?

409
00:33:15,702 --> 00:33:17,743
Wasn't he on the Vice Chairman's side?

410
00:33:17,743 --> 00:33:20,004
Looks like he flipped on him.

411
00:33:21,368 --> 00:33:23,466
Quiet down, everyone.

412
00:33:24,375 --> 00:33:27,993
We'll now move to a vote on the motion

413
00:33:27,993 --> 00:33:30,123
that Director Park has put forward.

414
00:33:30,123 --> 00:33:32,816
On the motion to appoint MD Jeon Seong Yeol

415
00:33:32,816 --> 00:33:35,295
as Co-Vice Chairman
alongside Vice Chairman Jeon Jae Yeol,

416
00:33:35,295 --> 00:33:37,355
all directors in favor,

417
00:33:37,355 --> 00:33:39,857
please raise your hands.

418
00:34:29,493 --> 00:34:31,142
Director Park.

419
00:34:31,142 --> 00:34:33,535
I owe this to you. I truly appreciate it.

420
00:34:33,535 --> 00:34:35,746
Time for me to get in line, too.

421
00:34:45,073 --> 00:34:46,160
Congratulations, Vice Chairman.

422
00:34:46,160 --> 00:34:48,535
Right, Ms. Joo.

423
00:34:48,535 --> 00:34:52,914
That last-minute surprise threw me off,
so it slipped my mind,

424
00:34:52,914 --> 00:34:55,380
but you mentioned you had something to report?

425
00:34:55,380 --> 00:34:58,641
Would you be submitting it in writing
or anything like that?

426
00:34:58,641 --> 00:35:00,505
No, there's nothing.

427
00:35:00,505 --> 00:35:03,427
All right then.

428
00:35:11,867 --> 00:35:13,909
Congratulations.

429
00:35:13,909 --> 00:35:15,870
I owe this to you.

430
00:35:17,368 --> 00:35:20,410
I look forward
to your continued guidance and support.

431
00:35:20,410 --> 00:35:22,402
The pleasure is all ours, sir...

432
00:35:22,402 --> 00:35:23,570
[This board meeting was wild]

433
00:35:23,570 --> 00:35:25,363
[Looks like Jeon Jae Yeol's people
all jumped ship to the new Vice Chairman]

434
00:35:25,363 --> 00:35:26,406
No way.

435
00:35:26,406 --> 00:35:28,783
Does this mean we need sign-off
from both Vice Chairmen now?

436
00:35:28,783 --> 00:35:31,411
Geez, who knows where this company is headed.

437
00:35:31,411 --> 00:35:34,082
Doesn't this make things pretty obvious?

438
00:35:34,082 --> 00:35:36,332
The smart move is hopping on the S side.

439
00:35:36,332 --> 00:35:38,793
So I caught wind of this
from the executive secretaries,

440
00:35:38,793 --> 00:35:41,629
Director Park had been
on the Vice Chairman's side from the start,

441
00:35:41,629 --> 00:35:44,301
but he turned on him this time around.

442
00:35:44,301 --> 00:35:46,991
Office politics are no joke.

443
00:35:46,991 --> 00:35:48,702
Hey, look how this turned out.

444
00:35:48,702 --> 00:35:50,430
What did? Who now?

445
00:35:50,430 --> 00:35:52,326
- Me?
- Be honest with me.

446
00:35:52,326 --> 00:35:54,533
I'm on your side.

447
00:36:00,618 --> 00:36:03,584
Yes, that report is...

448
00:37:00,152 --> 00:37:02,888
[Assistant Manager Noh Ki Jun]

449
00:37:25,702 --> 00:37:28,688
<i>The number you've reached is unavailable.
You'll be connected to voicemail</i>

450
00:37:28,688 --> 00:37:30,238
<i>after the tone, and standard rates apply...</i>

451
00:37:30,238 --> 00:37:32,154
[Joo In Ah]

452
00:38:09,669 --> 00:38:12,692
[Joo In Ah]

453
00:38:15,500 --> 00:38:18,294
[Joo In Ah]

454
00:39:12,993 --> 00:39:16,554
[Head of HR Bu Se Yeong]

455
00:39:20,181 --> 00:39:22,327
<i>Do you know what time it is?</i>

456
00:39:22,327 --> 00:39:23,821
Se Yeong.

457
00:39:24,784 --> 00:39:27,162
There's a favor I need from you.

458
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:33,147
Hey, how can this be sprung on me like this?

459
00:39:33,147 --> 00:39:34,988
Wasn't my U.S. assignment put on hold?

460
00:39:34,988 --> 00:39:37,328
Right, that was just because you were out sick,

461
00:39:37,328 --> 00:39:38,967
so now that you're back
on your feet, off you go.

462
00:39:38,967 --> 00:39:40,648
I'm not fully back to normal yet,

463
00:39:40,648 --> 00:39:42,028
and I've still got
outpatient treatment to deal with.

464
00:39:42,028 --> 00:39:44,288
There are hospitals in the U.S. too,
no need to worry.

465
00:39:44,288 --> 00:39:46,328
The company picks up all the medical bills.

466
00:39:46,328 --> 00:39:48,295
How great is that?

467
00:39:48,295 --> 00:39:49,627
So, has Ms. Joo been told?

468
00:39:49,627 --> 00:39:51,520
About this sudden reassignment?

469
00:39:52,201 --> 00:39:53,800
What are you talking about?

470
00:39:53,800 --> 00:39:56,159
- She's the one who asked for it.
- What?

471
00:39:56,159 --> 00:39:59,284
She wanted your U.S. assignment
fast-tracked as much as possible,

472
00:39:59,284 --> 00:40:01,025
called me at the crack of dawn.

473
00:40:01,025 --> 00:40:03,034
In exchange,
she wanted you promoted right away,

474
00:40:03,034 --> 00:40:06,938
placed at the top branch
and the most comfortable team.

475
00:40:06,938 --> 00:40:08,643
Looks like In Ah...

476
00:40:09,660 --> 00:40:11,854
really does care about you.

477
00:40:22,476 --> 00:40:24,794
[1g Gold Bar Giveaway]

478
00:40:33,019 --> 00:40:36,519
So everything up to this point
was already cleared in the last audit?

479
00:40:36,519 --> 00:40:39,118
Yes, and since there was
a major restructuring this time,

480
00:40:39,118 --> 00:40:40,880
I pulled up a brand-new sheet.

481
00:40:40,880 --> 00:40:43,572
I need a word with you.

482
00:40:44,432 --> 00:40:45,973
Can't you see I'm in the middle of a briefing?

483
00:40:45,973 --> 00:40:48,530
I said let's talk, right this minute!

484
00:40:54,692 --> 00:40:57,713
What's with this behavior?

485
00:40:59,741 --> 00:41:02,127
Hold off until Mr. Ahn is done.

486
00:41:13,152 --> 00:41:14,819
What did you want to say?

487
00:41:14,819 --> 00:41:16,499
Are you really asking like you don't know?

488
00:41:16,499 --> 00:41:18,539
What's going on with the U.S. assignment?

489
00:41:19,618 --> 00:41:21,932
Wasn't it already set for you to go?

490
00:41:21,932 --> 00:41:23,638
It's a great opportunity for you,

491
00:41:23,638 --> 00:41:25,809
and if you're heading there anyway,
sooner is better.

492
00:41:25,809 --> 00:41:28,243
At the California branch,
you'll get exposure to management work

493
00:41:28,243 --> 00:41:30,034
rather than just government relations.

494
00:41:30,034 --> 00:41:32,680
Forget all that. What's the real reason?

495
00:41:36,451 --> 00:41:37,867
Is this somehow...

496
00:41:39,118 --> 00:41:41,255
about J Care Foundation?

497
00:41:51,784 --> 00:41:54,811
I'm not such a clueless pushover
that I can't get the picture.

498
00:41:54,811 --> 00:41:56,159
I was actually beating myself up,

499
00:41:56,159 --> 00:41:59,029
wondering if I pushed you too hard.

500
00:41:59,029 --> 00:42:02,159
I mean, when an old classmate
you've barely heard from suddenly shows up

501
00:42:02,159 --> 00:42:04,723
asking for a single favor,
it's hard to turn down.

502
00:42:04,723 --> 00:42:08,352
You might feel inclined
to cover for an ex's slip-up.

503
00:42:08,352 --> 00:42:11,958
I regretted going overboard
because of my feelings.

504
00:42:13,784 --> 00:42:15,466
No, you weren't overreacting.

505
00:42:18,034 --> 00:42:19,911
I don't think...

506
00:42:21,743 --> 00:42:23,841
I can promise to set things right.

507
00:42:32,535 --> 00:42:33,833
Why not?

508
00:42:34,607 --> 00:42:36,168
Worried Jeon Jae Yeol might take a hit?

509
00:42:36,168 --> 00:42:38,263
Does that weigh on you that much?

510
00:42:40,076 --> 00:42:42,122
Are you going back to him?

511
00:42:42,122 --> 00:42:43,993
Like the Little Prince

512
00:42:43,993 --> 00:42:47,709
heading back to his planet
to see the rose he raised,

513
00:42:47,709 --> 00:42:50,644
is that what you're doing,
going back to Jeon Jae Yeol?

514
00:42:52,368 --> 00:42:54,912
- No, that's not it at all.
- Then...

515
00:42:55,816 --> 00:42:58,737
How on earth am I supposed
to make sense of all of this?

516
00:42:58,737 --> 00:43:00,176
Is it my job...

517
00:43:03,159 --> 00:43:05,547
to make you understand?

518
00:43:08,576 --> 00:43:11,623
You'll be busy prepping for the assignment,
so I'll pull you off duties for now.

519
00:43:11,623 --> 00:43:13,375
Get yourself ready.

520
00:43:14,606 --> 00:43:16,225
[Interview Room]

521
00:43:33,267 --> 00:43:34,282
Hey.

522
00:43:34,282 --> 00:43:35,723
Now that you're shipping off to the U.S.,

523
00:43:35,723 --> 00:43:37,523
you were really laying
into Ms. Joo, weren't you?

524
00:43:37,523 --> 00:43:39,735
Right? My jaw nearly hit the floor.

525
00:43:39,735 --> 00:43:43,015
By the way,
what were you two talking about earlier?

526
00:43:47,159 --> 00:43:49,450
Seriously, it's his own celebration,

527
00:43:49,450 --> 00:43:50,785
so why the long face?

528
00:43:50,785 --> 00:43:52,536
He's been doing nothing but downing shots.

529
00:43:52,536 --> 00:43:55,138
I know, right? On such a happy day.

530
00:43:55,826 --> 00:43:57,062
Oh come on, don't tell me

531
00:43:57,062 --> 00:43:59,463
you're sulking
because you don't want to buy us drinks?

532
00:43:59,463 --> 00:44:01,095
Oh, no way.

533
00:44:04,173 --> 00:44:05,635
Sounds good.

534
00:44:05,635 --> 00:44:08,597
And for next week's Jeju business trip,

535
00:44:08,597 --> 00:44:11,704
Ms. Joo, you should join us as well.

536
00:44:11,704 --> 00:44:13,157
Me?

537
00:44:13,923 --> 00:44:15,838
What's there for the Audit Office to support...

538
00:44:15,838 --> 00:44:18,190
During your assignment,
you worked on the CPK and JV deals.

539
00:44:18,190 --> 00:44:20,231
Bringing along a partner with experience

540
00:44:20,231 --> 00:44:22,743
would make the mood smoother.

541
00:44:22,743 --> 00:44:26,217
Then of course Ms. Joo has to be there.

542
00:44:26,217 --> 00:44:28,826
I'm jealous.

543
00:44:28,826 --> 00:44:31,633
Jeju must be amazing this time of year.

544
00:44:51,368 --> 00:44:53,739
<i>It's my birthday.</i>

545
00:44:56,228 --> 00:44:58,538
<i>How about giving it a try?</i>

546
00:45:02,818 --> 00:45:04,616
<i>What's this?</i>

547
00:45:24,004 --> 00:45:27,622
[Jeon Jae Yeol, Jeju]

548
00:45:41,118 --> 00:45:42,316
<i>Hello.</i>

549
00:45:42,316 --> 00:45:44,539
<i>Let's grab a drink. It's been ages.</i>

550
00:46:01,909 --> 00:46:04,186
You caught what was said
in the meeting earlier, right?

551
00:46:04,186 --> 00:46:05,567
Get next week's trip in order.

552
00:46:05,567 --> 00:46:08,130
Why Joo In Ah, of all people?

553
00:46:08,130 --> 00:46:10,587
There's plenty of reason for her to come along.

554
00:46:10,587 --> 00:46:12,679
She's also acquainted
with the experienced partner.

555
00:46:12,679 --> 00:46:14,856
Aside from that, the real reason.

556
00:46:16,166 --> 00:46:17,932
What are you trying to pull right now?

557
00:46:17,932 --> 00:46:20,509
What are you doing, Vice Chairman?

558
00:46:20,509 --> 00:46:21,909
You're picking fights while drunk,

559
00:46:21,909 --> 00:46:24,842
shipping off some employee overseas
because of personal feelings.

560
00:46:24,842 --> 00:46:27,566
Do you have any idea
what people are saying about you right now?

561
00:46:27,566 --> 00:46:31,381
That MD Jeon will end up as the head,
and you'll be pushed out.

562
00:46:31,381 --> 00:46:32,910
Do you walk away with minimal damage,

563
00:46:32,910 --> 00:46:34,450
or do you get stripped of everything
and tossed aside in disgrace?

564
00:46:34,450 --> 00:46:36,649
That's what everyone's buzzing about.

565
00:46:36,649 --> 00:46:39,339
So at a time like this,

566
00:46:39,339 --> 00:46:43,332
why can't you keep your own feelings in check
and stop slipping up?

567
00:46:43,332 --> 00:46:45,909
I've been used to that kind of talk for ages.

568
00:46:45,909 --> 00:46:47,829
And I have regrets.

569
00:46:47,829 --> 00:46:49,839
About letting it sway me,

570
00:46:49,839 --> 00:46:52,482
about not being honest with my own feelings.

571
00:46:54,660 --> 00:46:55,964
So what then?

572
00:46:55,964 --> 00:46:57,625
What are you planning to do,
following your heart?

573
00:46:57,625 --> 00:46:59,564
Are you going to die alongside Joo In Ah?

574
00:46:59,564 --> 00:47:01,984
After all, isn't she the woman you'd die with?

575
00:47:01,984 --> 00:47:05,085
The one getting emotional right now
seems to be you, not me.

576
00:47:05,085 --> 00:47:06,856
So?

577
00:47:06,856 --> 00:47:10,067
Could you give it all up? For her sake?

578
00:47:10,067 --> 00:47:11,918
If that's what it takes.

579
00:47:33,716 --> 00:47:35,528
What's this?

580
00:47:41,476 --> 00:47:44,078
What made me buy this?
Something I don't even use.

581
00:47:44,977 --> 00:47:49,039
From here on out,
I'm becoming a real minimalist.

582
00:47:52,326 --> 00:47:54,072
Hey, just leave that be.

583
00:47:54,072 --> 00:47:55,856
You think there are no dishes in the U.S.?

584
00:47:55,856 --> 00:47:58,216
Take it for yourself.

585
00:47:58,216 --> 00:47:59,909
Anyway, looking at it now,

586
00:47:59,909 --> 00:48:02,122
it worked out that you moved into this place.

587
00:48:02,122 --> 00:48:06,264
If I had to scramble for a tenant
while I'm off on the U.S. assignment...

588
00:48:09,201 --> 00:48:12,036
Hey, are you even listening?

589
00:48:12,036 --> 00:48:13,660
Ki Jun,

590
00:48:13,660 --> 00:48:16,463
did you know the Vice Chairman and Joo In Ah

591
00:48:16,463 --> 00:48:18,834
are heading to Jeju together next week?

592
00:48:20,702 --> 00:48:22,316
Yeah, I know.

593
00:48:22,316 --> 00:48:24,289
I checked the schedule.

594
00:48:24,289 --> 00:48:28,810
Jeju is where the two of them
took a trip together.

595
00:48:28,810 --> 00:48:31,284
That's how precious the memory is to him,

596
00:48:31,284 --> 00:48:34,417
he's even held
onto the plane tickets all this time.

597
00:48:36,657 --> 00:48:38,756
How modest of him.

598
00:48:38,756 --> 00:48:41,925
So even the rich go to Jeju
for a couple's trip.

599
00:48:44,951 --> 00:48:47,973
Hey, I told you to keep that cup for yourself.

600
00:48:48,850 --> 00:48:51,230
Did you pack everything in?

601
00:48:51,230 --> 00:48:54,437
Hey, set this dish up there too.

602
00:49:00,889 --> 00:49:02,654
You okay?

603
00:49:08,201 --> 00:49:09,536
I'll go get it.

604
00:49:09,536 --> 00:49:11,580
The food we ordered must be here.

605
00:49:26,867 --> 00:49:28,535
What?

606
00:49:28,535 --> 00:49:30,348
Ki Jun.

607
00:49:53,650 --> 00:49:55,562
I'll head out for a bit.

608
00:49:55,562 --> 00:49:57,828
- We're out of bottled water.
- Okay.

609
00:50:07,069 --> 00:50:08,141
What?

610
00:50:08,141 --> 00:50:09,421
Did I commit some kind of crime?

611
00:50:09,421 --> 00:50:10,461
I already explained the whole thing.

612
00:50:10,461 --> 00:50:12,676
I just lent her a room, that's all.

613
00:50:13,956 --> 00:50:16,055
Quit pinching me, will you?

614
00:50:18,569 --> 00:50:20,042
What kind of guy are you?

615
00:50:20,042 --> 00:50:21,806
You've got the woman
who stayed by your sickbed,

616
00:50:21,806 --> 00:50:23,363
and a separate woman
living with you on top of that?

617
00:50:23,363 --> 00:50:24,643
Who do you think you are?
What gives you the right?

618
00:50:24,643 --> 00:50:26,882
I don't have the right.

619
00:50:26,882 --> 00:50:28,650
But here's the thing,

620
00:50:29,944 --> 00:50:32,429
she says she doesn't have feelings for me.

621
00:50:32,429 --> 00:50:34,348
What kind of nonsense are you talking?

622
00:50:34,348 --> 00:50:38,076
How would she act like that
if she didn't have feelings, huh?

623
00:50:38,769 --> 00:50:39,815
I don't know. That's what she's saying.

624
00:50:39,815 --> 00:50:41,362
She says she's into another guy.

625
00:50:41,362 --> 00:50:43,331
So you'd better drop it too.

626
00:50:46,029 --> 00:50:47,095
You complete dimwit.

627
00:50:47,865 --> 00:50:50,345
How can you only go by what she's saying?

628
00:50:50,345 --> 00:50:52,366
Her behavior, expressions,
that look in her eyes,

629
00:50:52,366 --> 00:50:54,581
those are what you should be watching!

630
00:50:54,581 --> 00:50:57,413
Hey, that look in her eyes
while watching you sick? That one?

631
00:50:57,413 --> 00:50:59,209
Oh my gosh!

632
00:50:59,209 --> 00:51:01,086
This is so frustrating.

633
00:51:09,028 --> 00:51:10,861
It's a pleasure, by the way.

634
00:51:10,861 --> 00:51:13,069
Pleasure to meet you, too.

635
00:51:13,069 --> 00:51:16,239
- Nice to see you again.
- Nice to see you again.

636
00:51:20,195 --> 00:51:22,487
I'm glad you like it.

637
00:51:22,487 --> 00:51:24,748
You should try this.

638
00:52:53,365 --> 00:52:57,054
<i>There's this weird thing
where at crucial moments...</i>

639
00:52:57,658 --> 00:53:00,531
<i>I end up hiding what I really feel.</i>

640
00:53:23,851 --> 00:53:25,853
Where's the place in Jeju?

641
00:53:25,853 --> 00:53:26,511
<i>What?</i>

642
00:53:26,511 --> 00:53:28,750
I'm asking where in Jeju Joo In Ah is staying.

643
00:53:28,750 --> 00:53:29,990
Why are you asking,

644
00:53:29,990 --> 00:53:31,431
planning to chase her all the way out there?

645
00:53:31,431 --> 00:53:33,752
I asked you where, right now.

646
00:53:35,770 --> 00:53:38,048
Jeon Jae Yeol, Noh Ki Jun...

647
00:53:39,445 --> 00:53:42,093
both of you have totally lost it.

648
00:53:55,549 --> 00:53:57,262
The terms aren't half bad,

649
00:53:57,262 --> 00:53:59,428
though some fleshing out is needed.

650
00:53:59,428 --> 00:54:02,615
Still, I'd like the investment size
to be a bit larger.

651
00:54:02,615 --> 00:54:04,603
That brings bigger risk along with it.

652
00:54:04,603 --> 00:54:06,563
For CPK, it's all just playing
with money anyway.

653
00:54:06,563 --> 00:54:08,578
There's no soul in it.

654
00:54:15,320 --> 00:54:17,545
Coming back feels good.

655
00:54:21,245 --> 00:54:22,841
Jeju, I mean,

656
00:54:23,789 --> 00:54:27,505
it was our first and last trip together.

657
00:54:28,897 --> 00:54:32,122
We worked hard to line up the vacation
and took the plunge,

658
00:54:32,836 --> 00:54:35,372
yet even back then,
all we did was work like this.

659
00:54:39,320 --> 00:54:41,390
The board composition is what worries me most.

660
00:54:41,390 --> 00:54:42,974
In Ah.

661
00:54:48,111 --> 00:54:51,271
It seems you're having trouble focusing,

662
00:54:51,271 --> 00:54:53,857
so I'll review it on my own
and report back to you separately.

663
00:54:53,857 --> 00:54:55,834
In Ah, hold on a second.

664
00:54:57,111 --> 00:54:58,882
For just a moment, the two of us,

665
00:55:00,403 --> 00:55:02,671
couldn't we be the way we used to?

666
00:55:09,403 --> 00:55:11,289
That's never going to happen,

667
00:55:12,522 --> 00:55:14,778
us going back to the way we used to be.

668
00:55:14,778 --> 00:55:16,992
Then why did you come back to Korea?

669
00:55:28,019 --> 00:55:29,351
Loyalty.

670
00:55:30,834 --> 00:55:33,445
That promise I made to stand by your side,

671
00:55:34,148 --> 00:55:35,941
this is the last bit of loyalty I owe to it.

672
00:55:35,941 --> 00:55:37,279
It's enough for me.

673
00:55:37,279 --> 00:55:40,348
It doesn't matter
if it's loyalty or some other feeling,

674
00:55:41,514 --> 00:55:43,520
just stay right here by my side,

675
00:55:44,411 --> 00:55:45,880
that's all I need.

676
00:55:52,778 --> 00:55:54,856
I won't be doing even that anymore.

677
00:55:56,027 --> 00:55:58,247
Being held captive by that promise,

678
00:56:00,344 --> 00:56:02,578
I made a mistake I shouldn't have made.

679
00:56:04,944 --> 00:56:07,192
And I hurt someone,

680
00:56:09,478 --> 00:56:11,753
someone I should never have hurt.

681
00:56:15,403 --> 00:56:17,916
Are you talking about Mr. Noh?

682
00:56:29,361 --> 00:56:31,263
So that's why I'm telling you,

683
00:56:32,179 --> 00:56:34,856
I'm never coming back to you.

684
00:58:00,756 --> 00:58:03,759
It must be too late, right?

685
00:58:03,759 --> 00:58:06,065
For me to come to you.

686
00:58:11,850 --> 00:58:13,990
Joo In Ah!

687
00:58:36,976 --> 00:58:38,973
Joo In Ah!

688
00:58:55,561 --> 00:58:57,700
Noh Ki Jun...

689
00:59:13,042 --> 00:59:16,476
Why on earth did you check out so soon,

690
00:59:16,476 --> 00:59:19,097
after I went all the way out to that hotel...

691
01:01:03,339 --> 01:01:05,824
[Haemu Audit Team 3]

692
01:01:09,212 --> 01:01:13,677
[Joo In Ah is in an inappropriate relationship
with a coworker]

693
01:01:15,223 --> 01:01:17,575
[Joo In Ah is in an inappropriate relationship
with a coworker]

694
01:01:26,466 --> 01:01:30,089
[Send]

695
01:01:30,113 --> 01:01:33,091
[Filing For Love]

696
01:02:01,694 --> 01:02:03,415
<i>By the way, something's been bothering me,</i>

697
01:02:03,415 --> 01:02:06,799
<i>how obvious my feelings for you
might be at work.</i>

698
01:02:07,541 --> 01:02:09,195
<i>Clear your whole weekend.</i>

699
01:02:09,195 --> 01:02:10,835
<i>I've booked a pool villa in Sokcho.</i>

700
01:02:10,835 --> 01:02:13,463
<i>Then you should go
to Mr. Min's club event this weekend.</i>

701
01:02:13,463 --> 01:02:14,265
<i>What?</i>

702
01:02:14,265 --> 01:02:16,049
<i>You said you'd be on fire
once we started dating,</i>

703
01:02:16,049 --> 01:02:17,705
<i>but you're firing work at me
like flames instead.</i>

704
01:02:17,705 --> 01:02:20,704
<i>Want to stay for some ramyeon?</i>

705
01:02:20,704 --> 01:02:22,385
<i>Must be fun for you, isn't it,</i>

706
01:02:22,385 --> 01:02:23,727
<i>stuck between two men?</i>

707
01:02:23,727 --> 01:02:24,991
<i>I'm getting a divorce.</i>

708
01:02:24,991 --> 01:02:26,980
<i>I have regrets about everything.</i>

709
01:02:26,980 --> 01:02:28,909
<i>What are you doing here?</i>
